  "notes": "The research calls him \"the deliberate crossover exception\" and that phrase is the model: major and Mixolydian as often as minor, which no other entry on this axis carries at equal weight, plus the fastest tempo band here outside The Bomb Squad at 95–105. The second parameter is arena carry — a snare layered with a clap, tambourine on 8ths in hooks and handclap breakdowns \"designed for crowd participation\" — so `velocityTiers` runs near the top of this axis, the clap offset is wide, and `openHat.prob` is 0.35. The third is the hook mechanism, and it is the reason the countermelody matters here: \"the hook is a crowd chant doubling the loop's top line\" is literally `octave_echo` at double weight with `fillGapsOnly` off and `densityRatio` 0.6. Bass is root–5th–octave motion \"mixed forward\", which is `mirror_kick` loosened to `followRootsProb` 0.7 with P5 and P8 passing tones rather than a walking line. ⚠ `medium` and the research says medium too — the sample documentation is song-level and the producer interview is weighted toward his R&B work rather than the Naughty records. The specific inferred parameter is `session.bpm.mode` at 99: the 95–105 band is catalog-level and the centre inside it is this author's. ⚠ The I–vi–IV–V family is INFERRED and carries the lowest weight; the research names I–IV, I–V–vi–IV and i–VII–VI. ⚠ `countermelody.fillGapsOnly` returned to true. With it off and a density of 0.6, the counter plays THROUGH the melody rather than around it, and coherence.rs measures that as the counter sounding the melody own pitch at the same moment — a second lead rather than an answer. The register offset and the styles are untouched; what changed is that it waits its turn.",
